approval/asked 1->2 sha256:ea2887bc7de46faa21f3dcccf92f8f462288cfeb5de04e845204bd3a255c9d39 kind (approval or consent, required), the optional subject and the optional sandbox mode added (M1-D-PIPE-1 A, plan 16.1.2, Rule 6); a version-1 record has no kind, so the version is bumped; upgrade 1 sets kind "approval"
approval/decided 1->2 sha256:52af1ea31e16ace82fb52bc4b458932f0c9adca9c27ac5e141bc0bf4bc1da365 the outcome vocabulary is M1-D-PIPE-1 A's five (allowed-once, allowed-by-grant, rejected, cancelled, unavailable), by gained the optional peer and the optional grant names the grant used or created (plan 16.1.2, Rule 6); an older binary refuses the new outcomes, so the version is bumped; upgrade 1 maps approved to allowed-once (allowed-by-grant when its detail names the grant), denied to rejected (cancelled for a cancellation, unavailable for the harness's own refusals), timeout to unavailable with detail timeout, no-answerer to unavailable, and moves a grant id from the detail to grant
